{
  "_comment": "RBC/G36 AHU collection (Ghalamsiah et al.; simulated 114-feature schema shared by 03_RBC-5wk and the 04-08 G36 folders) point -> CAMBER Role mapping, and the equipment each column belongs to: each run splits into the air handler AHU and its five VAV zones AHU_VAV_<East|South|West|North|Core> (run group 'mapping'); zone ids nest under the AHU id, so the naming topology groups each scenario's zones under that scenario's AHU. Every mapped header is listed in all three published spellings: UTF-8 '(°K)' (04/05/06/08), the same text in Latin-1 (03_RBC-5wk, read with encoding latin-1, which also renames the South/North discharge-air and the fan-speed columns) and '(Â°K)' (07_G36-Cyber, a double-encoded degree sign). The OA damper is the TRUE position column (the stuck position when a stuck fault is injected; otherwise the BAS command), the cooling / heating valves are the BAS control signals (the controller's demand, as in the LBNL mappings). The zone 'VAV Damper Position' is the damper; the zone 'VAV Damper Control Signal' is NOT mapped: it tracks airflow (corr 0.98-1.00, a constant flow/signal ratio per zone) -- a normalised airflow setpoint, not a damper command (data issue zone-damper-signal-is-airflow-setpoint). OCC_<zone> / FAN_<zone> are CAMBER copies (derive 'copy') of the AHU's occupied-mode and fan-status points, so the zone census rules gate their request cycles on the system being on. Not mapped: zone reheat (a W power signal, not a valve), mass flows (kg/s, no CAMBER unit; sign convention differs by folder), plant points, coil heat rates and powers. Units: K (temperatures), m3/s (zone airflow), Pa (static), fraction (positions, speeds) -- declared on the catalog entry. Dataset: Ghalamsiah et al. 2026, Sci Data (doi:10.1038/s41597-025-06179-y), CC-BY-4.0.",
